  "body": "### Summary\nAs a member upgrading from the legacy app, I want one malformed smiley favourite, search entry, upload or draft to be skipped, so that the rest of my list is still imported. Today the whole list is refused and the step is marked done for good.\n\n### Scenario\nA legacy `smiley_favorites_cache2` with one favourite lacking `dateAdded`, or an upload-history entry with a null `fullURL`: the step answers `.failed(.sourceUnreadable)`, which counts as finished, and nothing of that list is ever imported. **Not established:** that legacy can write such an entry; cite a legacy `file:line` @ `87fe0d1c` or a capture before fixing.\n\n### Evidence (`7a61018f`)\n- `Packages/HFRKit/Sources/HFRStorage/LegacyImport/LegacyFormats.swift:149-153`: inside the loop over favourites, `guard … let date = KeyedArchive.date(favorite[\"dateAdded\"], in: objects) else { return nil }` aborts the list.\n- Same file `:72-74`, `:89-90`, `:112-114`: `searchHistory`, `uploadHistory`, `activeDrafts` decode `[Entry]` in one `try?`.\n- Same file `:124-129`: `pseudoList` does the opposite and skips a bad entry with `compactMap`.\n- `LegacyImport/LegacyImportReport.swift:57-61`: `.failed(.sourceUnreadable)` is `isDone`.\n\n### Fix\nSkip the malformed entry, count it in `report.rejectedItems`, import the rest; keep `sourceUnreadable` for a file that is not the expected container.\n\n### Test (fails before the fix)\n`LegacyFormatsTests/aFavouriteWithoutADateIsSkippedNotTheWholeArchive`: an archive of three favourites, one without `dateAdded`, yields two (today nil).\n\nRework model: Sonnet 5.5, reviewed by Opus 5.5.\n\nFound by #775 (cloud/r775-fable, Fable 5.2). Reviewed at `dev-swift` @ `7a61018f`; read from the code, not run on a device unless stated.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
