   "body": "**cloud/m4q-reliab-opus: not fixed. The issue's precondition (\"cite a legacy `file:line` @ `87fe0d1c` or a capture before fixing\") does not hold; read at `87fe0d1c`.**\n\nLegacy never writes a malformed entry in these four lists, and for three of them legacy's own reader already drops the whole list:\n- **Smiley search history**: `HFRswift/Swift/SmileySearchService.swift:78-83`, `SmileySearchHistoryEntry` is `Codable` with non-optional `text`, `count`, `lastDate`, written with `JSONEncoder`; legacy reads it back with `try? JSONDecoder().decode([SmileySearchHistoryEntry].self, …)` (`:92-96`), all or nothing, as our port does.\n- **Upload history**: `ReplyService.swift:1855-1876`: `fullURL: String` and `timeStamp: Date` are non-optional, so `JSONEncoder` cannot write a null `fullURL`.\n- **Active drafts**: same shape (Codable, non-optional), so the same argument applies.\n- **Smiley favourites**: the only writer, `Classes/SmileyCache.m:400-404`, sets `sCode`, `sRawUrl` and `dateAdded = [NSDate now]` on every entry (callers: `SmileyAlertView.m:106`; `ReplySmileyCatalog.swift:94`, whose arguments are non-optional Swift `String`s). An entry with a nil field would not survive legacy either: `loadDicFavorties` builds `[NSArray arrayWithObjects:sf.sRawUrl, sf.sCode, nil]` (`SmileyCache.m:381`), which a nil `sRawUrl` truncates, so `dictionaryWithObjects:forKeys:` raises on the count mismatch.\n\nSo the current all-or-nothing import matches what legacy itself could read, and no captured legacy state reaches the failing path. Making the import skip a bad entry would be defensive code for a state nobody has shown to exist (AGENTS §3 \"no guessing\"; ESSENTIEL \"never guess\").\n\nOptions for the operator:\n- **(a)** Close as not reproducible.\n- **(b)** Keep it as a defensive hardening (`needs-decision`): skip and count in `rejectedItems`. This is cheap and changes no valid import.\n- **(c)** A Mac capture of a real legacy store showing such an entry.\n\nI have not claimed it; the orchestrator decides.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
